+# AW-12: integrator ownership correction after B7
+
+Review in progress. The original B7 result is **282 passed, nine failed** in
+independent verification, 159.69 seconds. Its source hash was
+`8b670a0cdde7660abdfa3c96b16a968d52c59d7acb86caba4616f8de1001e953`,
+unchanged before and after the final review checks. The original worker patch
+is retained as `patches/av5m4b7-grok-original-2026-09-08.patch` (300,847 bytes).
+These corrections are Astra's review work, not Grok's original output.
+
+Three additional cases failed in **3.77 seconds** on those original bytes:
+
+- A real originating thread exited while its writer remained alive. Simulating
+  integer-ID reuse at the mirror module's query let a different thread replace
+  the original intent through writer PID 67980. The actual current ID was
+  70136 and the simulated ID 57204. Windows allocator reuse was not observed;
+  the live writer and changed intent were observed.
+- Cancelling a prepared session with no child returned false and kept both
+  retention and the gate. Competitor PID 68488 was refused. No future launch
+  was needed to establish that the already-cancelled session could not start.
+- Cancellation closed job handle 644 while the launcher was paused before
+  assigning launcher PID 10992 to it. The probe prevented a kernel call with
+  the known stale handle. No such invalid kernel call or post-timeout
+  publication is claimed. Original-session cleanup confirmed physical death.
+
+## Repair recorded before rerun
+
+Helper authority now uses the original Thread object; the integer ID remains
+diagnostic metadata. Python explicitly permits integer IDs to be recycled
+([threading reference](https://docs.python.org/3/library/threading.html#threading.get_ident)).
+Existing operation context and originating-helper controls remain intact.
+
+Prepared-only cancellation clears pending launch and releases after proven
+absence of a child. Launch rechecks cancellation under the same state lock.
+The in-progress handoff stays owned through job assignment, including after
+Popen returns its process object. Cancellation during that handoff returns
+without closing the launcher's job. State locks do not span Popen or pipe
+reads. Later child-job assignment checks cancellation under the state lock.
+
+A nonblocking termination lock gives native-job cleanup one owner. Concurrent
+cancel requests mark admission dead and return false while that owner finishes.
+Graceful shutdown delegates final cleanup to the same path. The redundant
+second job close on the Popen exception path is removed. This prevents the
+same ownership problem from moving to overlapping termination calls.
+
+The three original probes are unchanged in the new AW-12 acceptance files.
+One new test observes concurrent termination, bounded second-caller return,
+retained exclusion and a single job close. Run the unchanged full B7 union
+plus these four cases in the worker and checkout before integration.
+
+The first corrected-source focus passed **11 tests**, 13.25 seconds. It includes
+all four new AW-12 cases, the unchanged three AW-11 cases and all four B7 cases.
+The prepared cancellation released the gate, the assignment handoff retained
+its job, and concurrent termination closed the job exactly once. All original
+failed observations remain retained separately.
+
+The full corrected union passed **286 tests with nine frozen failures**,
+168.87 seconds, in the worktree. Mirror SHA-256 remained
+`33bd644ca3ac13070716fa8493221260c4b713ba71e4a402683d608de06761b3`.
+Checkout verification and integration commit are pending. The nine frozen
+Phase 4 failures remain failed, and actual client acceptance is still pending.
